I agree, for my part. I made a genocideless ascension to learn how to 
deal with mind flayers and liches, especially during an ascension run.

I am working on a wishless ascension now, because I noticed that in my 
previous 5 ascensions a great number of wishes generally contributed. 
I'd like to learn how to beat the game without depending on the WoW in 
the castle. It can be done, and learning how will definately make me a 
better player.

As for wizards, I have 2 wizard ascensions under my belt. Wizards are 
hands down my favorite class. The trick is to not worry about the pet - 
get as much xp as you can, as fast as you can. Doing so builds up spell 
power, which compensates for other shortcomings. It certainly helps to 
have a sleep spell or even an identify spell, but it isn't required. 
Make liberal use of the force bolt spell to kill things at a distance.

If the levels of the main dungeon seem to be getting too risky, its time 
to head to the up stairs and go to the gnome mines - but just to 
minetown, not all the way. Then go back and find Sokoban.

And get magicbane as fast as you can. Also, I never #enhance my staff 
slots, because its just a waste. Id rather use my enhancements on spells 
and dagger.

